{
 "id": "synthetic-g36-rcx-chains",
 "title": "Synthetic G36 fleet with faults that propagate from an air handler to its boxes (generated by CAMBER)",
 "summary": "SYNTHETIC, generated locally by CAMBER (no download, no real building): the G36 VAV fleet of synthetic-g36-vav-fleet (six single-duct reheat boxes per air handler under trim-and-respond resets), with each air handler's supply fan speed and cooling valve, hourly for three weeks of spring, as five air handlers: a healthy one, a healthy one with one stuck box damper, a cooling coil that cannot make supply air below 63 F, a weak supply fan that cannot make more than 0.35 in. w.c., and a SAT reset disabled at 55 F with two single-maximum reheat boxes. A declared served-by topology ties each box to its air handler, so the RCx report roots the boxes' symptoms on the air handler that causes them.",
 "teaches": [
  "how the RCx report's AHU-to-VAV cause chains turn many box findings into one air-handler issue (\"4 of 6 boxes\")",
  "why a box's own fault stays its own issue when its air handler is healthy",
  "why a chain's cost is its largest member, never the sum of its members"
 ],
 "publisher": "CAMBER (generated locally by the user's copy)",
